The U.S. state of [[Oregon]] first required its residents to register their [[motor vehicle]]s in 1905. Registrants provided their own [[Vehicle registration plate|license plate]]s for display until 1911, when the state began to issue plates.<ref>{{cite web |title=Old Oregon License Plates |url=http://leatherlicenseplates.com/old-oregon-license-plates-vintage-oregon-license-plates/ |publisher=LeatherLicensePlates.com |date=<!-- Deny Citation Bot--> |access-date=August 17, 2017}}</ref>

{{As of|2022}}, plates are issued by the [[Oregon Department of Transportation]] through its Driver & Motor Vehicle Services branch. Front and rear plates are required for most classes of vehicles, while only rear plates are required for motorcycles and trailers.

